WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.680
How Google finds your page, and the free tools to check it.

2
00:00:04.030 --> 00:00:07.510
This is the video for module one of the SEO course.

3
00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:11.810
SEO stands for search engine optimisation.

4
00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:20.520
It means making a website easier for search engines to find, understand and show to the right people, without paying for each click.

5
00:00:21.770 --> 00:00:28.250
When a woman in Ibadan types tailor near Bodija, the businesses that appear first did not get there by luck.

6
00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:36.310
In this video you will learn how that happens, how to check a page yourself, and how to set up your free tools safely.

7
00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:44.860
Stage one is crawling. Google uses automatic programs called crawlers. Google's crawler is called Googlebot.

8
00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:52.270
Crawlers find new pages mainly by following links, and from sitemaps, which are files that list a site's pages.

9
00:00:53.520 --> 00:01:03.350
Stage two is indexing. Google reads the text, headings, images and title, and may store the page in its index, a huge database of pages.

10
00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:09.290
Copies, very thin pages and pages with a noindex instruction are usually left out.

11
00:01:10.540 --> 00:01:18.350
Stage three is serving results. When someone searches, Google returns the pages it thinks are most relevant and useful.

12
00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:28.430
So remember this. A page can only rank after it has been crawled and indexed. A problem early in the flow blocks everything after it.

13
00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:39.880
For example, Ngozi runs a small chops business in Lekki, Lagos. Her designer added a party packs page two weeks ago, but she cannot find it on Google.

14
00:01:41.130 --> 00:01:51.580
She types site, colon, then her domain into Google. This special search shows pages Google has indexed from her site. She sees 6 results, but not party packs.

15
00:01:52.830 --> 00:01:58.630
She searches the exact page address the same way. No results. It is not in the index yet.

16
00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:05.900
She checks her home page and menu. Nothing links to the new page, so crawlers have no path to it.

17
00:02:07.150 --> 00:02:14.660
She asks the designer to add a Party Packs link to the menu and home page, and to submit the sitemap in Search Console.

18
00:02:15.910 --> 00:02:20.090
Ten days later the page appears. The fix was links and a sitemap.

19
00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:30.300
You can control whether your pages can be crawled, what they say, how fast and mobile friendly they are, and how your Google Business Profile looks.

20
00:02:31.550 --> 00:02:36.990
You cannot control Google's ranking systems, your competitors, or how many people search.

21
00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:45.110
Nobody can guarantee a number one position. Google itself warns site owners to be careful of anyone who promises that.

22
00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:52.950
First, turn on 2-Step Verification, so a stolen password alone cannot open your Google account.

23
00:02:54.200 --> 00:03:06.980
Next, go to Search Console and add your site. A Domain property covers every version of the site. A URL prefix property covers one exact address and offers more ways to verify.

24
00:03:08.230 --> 00:03:19.580
Verify ownership. For example, Chioma had only a phone. She pasted the HTML tag code into her Yoast SEO settings in WordPress, and tapped Verify.

25
00:03:20.830 --> 00:03:27.420
Then open the Sitemaps report and submit your sitemap address. Chioma's took about 20 minutes in total.

26
00:03:28.670 --> 00:03:41.340
Finally, if a designer or volunteer helps you, never share your password. Add them as a user with Full or Restricted permission, and remove their access the same day they stop working with you.

27
00:03:42.590 --> 00:03:53.320
Small businesses get many scam messages. The first promises guaranteed number one on Google in 7 days. Google's own advice says no one can guarantee that.

28
00:03:54.570 --> 00:04:02.210
The second offers to sell thousands of backlinks or reviews. Buying them breaks Google's policies and can harm your site.

29
00:04:03.460 --> 00:04:08.130
The third claims your site will be removed from Google unless you pay. Do not pay.

30
00:04:09.380 --> 00:04:12.370
Tick every item before you start changing pages.

31
00:04:12.720 --> 00:04:23.210
Then write down a baseline: clicks and impressions for the last 28 days, and your top five searches. Without a starting point, you cannot prove your work made a difference.

32
00:04:24.460 --> 00:04:39.550
To remember. Google crawls, indexes, then serves. Crawlers find pages through links and sitemaps. Use the site search for a quick check. Protect your account and never share passwords. And nobody can guarantee a top position.

33
00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:51.400
Now try it. Run a site search on a website you know, map five customer searches to their intent, then verify a site in Search Console and submit its sitemap.

34
00:04:51.750 --> 00:04:53.690
Continue with the lessons below.
